{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation complete (pending Gerrit review). Design decisions of note:\n\n1. Marker ownership: `evidence_sufficient:false` is written ONLY by the framework — the bounded fallback now calls a new `CriterionBank.record_insufficient()` (source=\"fallback\") instead of the model-facing record tool, so the tool stays bool-only and a tool met=false remains a positive refutation. `harvest_structured_into_bank` ignores any model-supplied marker and preserves a prior entry's marker on a markerless met=false overwrite (met=true clears it).\n\n2. Module-size cap: completion_banking.py was at 799/800 LOC, so the verdict-assembly cluster (assemble_deterministic_verdict, merge_finalizer_with_bank, ticket_id_of, _findings_for_unmet) was extracted along its existing call-graph seam into new completion_verdict_assembly.py (258 LOC) with re-exports from completion_banking — no caller changes. banking is now 660 LOC.\n\n3. Authoritative re-stamp: merge_finalizer_with_bank re-stamps EVERY record from its bank entry via _restamp_marker (stamps a still-unmet echo over a marked entry; strips model-minted markers over bare entries or met=true). Deterministic assembly and both placeholder branches carry the marker; findings say \"insufficient evidence\", not refutation.\n\n4. reconcile_verdict derives the top-level marker (never trusts model output): set iff FAIL, >=1 unmet record carries the per-criterion marker, and NO unmet record lacks it; such a FAIL carries a new INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE_REMEDIATION instead of the generic guidance. PASS pops both. The 2a6f verdict_obtainable fault path is untouched (pinned by test).\n\n5. Sidecar FAIL payload now records `criteria` (previously omitted) plus the top-level marker, mirroring the verdict_obtainable block, so an insufficiency FAIL is diagnosable from the durable record. close_precheck refusal still raises fail-closed but reports \"insufficient evidence for N criteria (nothing positively refuted)\" when marked. Renderer wording likewise.\n\n6. Complexity ratchet: extracting _verification_fail_message dropped _completion_precheck below the McCabe threshold entirely — the frozen ceiling entry became stale and was removed via the sanctioned shrink-only `--update-stale` path (a decrease, not a bump).\n\nValidation: withheld-oracle TDD — new tests/unit/workflow/test_insufficient_evidence_marker.py (31 tests) written first, 24 failed on unmodified code / 7 regression guards passed; all green after. Manual mutation pass: 24 mutants across every changed function, 24/24 killed. make lint, make typecheck, complexity check (new=0 increased=0 stale=0) all green. Full unit suite: 10368 passed; the only failures are the known environmental git-remote/bare-repo class (fail identically on a clean tree)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786736237671759001,"uuid":"e1b7cda6-4fbb-4cec-a813-6b7a9a5e2de0"}